    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0111",
      "sequence": 966,
      "meaning": "The gods continue their hymn: victory to Rāma, eternal abode and remover of sorrow, lord of Raghu armed with bow and arrows, the lion who tears apart the elephant of worldly existence. They celebrate his limitless beauty and virtues, his destruction of Rāvaṇa like Garuḍa seizing a great serpent, his generosity in incarnation, his ending of earth’s burden, his crowning of destitute Vibhīṣaṇa and his skill in destroying the wicked. They bow to the beginningless, pervasive, stainless Lord with Ramā; to the charming red-eyed king whose bow and arrows remove grave faults born in the mind; and to the reality that the Vedas call at once every form and beyond every form, distinct yet undivided like the sun and its light. Declaring the monkeys fulfilled while a divine body without devotion is contemptible, they ask Rāma to remove their divisive understanding, destroy conduct that mistakes pain for pleasure, and grant perpetual auspicious love for his lotus feet.",
