    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0112",
      "sequence": 967,
      "meaning": "At that moment Daśaratha arrives and his eyes fill with tears at sight of his son. Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa bow, and their father blesses them, saying Rāma’s merit has conquered the unconquerable demon king. Hearing his son’s words, Daśaratha’s love deepens until tears rise and his hair stands on end. Raghupati recognizes that love and graciously gives his father firm knowledge. Śiva explains that Daśaratha nevertheless does not choose liberation, for his mind rests in loving distinction; worshippers of the embodied Lord do not take release, and Rāma grants them devotion to himself. Repeatedly bowing, Daśaratha joyfully returns to the gods’ realm.",
