    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0115",
      "sequence": 970,
      "meaning": "Śiva prays for protection from Rāma, handsome bow and excellent arrow in hand, as the wind that scatters the massive cloud of delusion, the fire that consumes the forest of doubt and the sun whose majesty dispels the darkness of error. Both beyond qualities and manifest with qualities, he is the lion before the elephants of desire, anger and pride and is asked to dwell always in his servant’s heart-forest. He is a killing frost to the lotus-bed of sense-born wishes, the Mandara that churns the ocean of becoming, the one who averts and carries across difficult transmigration. Śiva asks the dark, lotus-eyed friend of the lowly to dwell with Jānakī and Lakṣmaṇa within his heart, and calls him delight of sages, ornament of earth and destroyer of Tulsīdāsa’s fear.",
