      "sequence": 971,
      "meaning": "After Śiva offers his prayer and departs, Vibhīṣaṇa approaches, bows and petitions the gentle bow-bearing Lord. Rāma has slain Rāvaṇa with his clan and army and spread purifying fame through the three worlds, while showing manifold grace to one so poor, impure, low-minded and low-born as Vibhīṣaṇa. He asks the Lord to sanctify his servant’s house, bathe away the fatigue of battle, inspect the treasury, palace and wealth, and gladly bestow riches upon the monkeys. Above all, he begs Rāma to adopt him fully and take him along to Ayodhyā. Hearing the humble words, the compassionate Lord’s two great eyes fill with tears.",
